<%# Mashups page: three live integrations, each combining Lpaecomms' own
    catalogue or forms with an external service. The page itself carries no
    data — every card fetches from /api/v1 in the browser, which is the same
    contract the mobile and desktop clients use. Wrapped by layouts/base.ejs. %>

<%# Centred hero, from the Marshup mockup. The mockup spells it "Marshup";
    the nav, the routes and the docs all say Mashups, so the page keeps the
    spelling the rest of the site uses. %>
<section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl pb-14 pt-10 text-center sm:pb-16 sm:pt-16">
  <span class="text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent">
    Integrations, built on one API
  </span>
  <h1 class="mt-5 font-display text-4xl font-bold leading-[1.15] tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">
    Mashups
  </h1>
  <p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
    A mashup blends data or services from more than one source into a single
    view. Each card below combines the Lpaecomms catalogue with an external
    service, live in your browser.
  </p>
</section>

<%# Each mashup is its own component under views/components/mashup. The paths
    are literal so a wrong name fails loudly at include time and stays
    greppable. None of them takes locals: their data arrives over the API. %>
<section class="flex flex-col gap-7 pb-24">
  <%- include('../components/mashup/mashupOne') %>
  <%- include('../components/mashup/mashupTwo') %>
  <%- include('../components/mashup/mashupThree') %>
</section>
